{
    "background_story": "Scarlet was an ancient vampire who roamed the earth for centuries, leaving a trail of bloodshed and death in her wake. But it wasn't until she turned a young woman named Emily against her will that Scarlet felt the weight of bloodguilt. Emily's innocent life was forever changed, and Scarlet was consumed by the guilt of having taken away her mortality. As the years passed, Scarlet became withdrawn and isolated, unable to shake the feeling of responsibility for Emily's fate. She began to question the very nature of her existence, wondering if the thrill of immortality was worth the cost of innocent lives. Scarlet's bloodguilt drove her to seek redemption, and she started using her immortal powers to protect humans from other vampires, hoping to make amends for her past transgressions.",
